          "en": "Paragraph 1 of Article 182 of the Criminal Law is amended to read: Whoever manipulates the securities or futures market under any of the following circumstances, thereby affecting the prices of securities or futures trading or the volume of securities or futures trading, if the circumstances are serious, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than five years or criminal detention, and shall also, or shall only, be fined; if the circumstances are especially serious, he shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than five years and not more than ten years, and shall be fined:\n(a) independently or in collusion with others, concentrating advantages in funds, shareholdings or positions, or taking advantage of advantages in information, to buy or sell securities jointly or continuously;\n(b) colluding with another person to trade securities or futures with each other at a pre-agreed time, price and method;\n(c) conducting securities transactions between accounts actually controlled by himself, or buying and selling futures contracts with himself as the counterparty;\n(d) frequently or in large quantities placing and then cancelling orders to buy or sell securities or futures contracts without the purpose of concluding transactions;\n(e) inducing investors to conduct securities or futures trading by using false or uncertain major information;\n(f) publicly making an evaluation, prediction or investment recommendation on a security, a securities issuer or the underlying asset of futures trading, while conducting reverse securities trading or related futures trading; or\n(g) manipulating the securities or futures market by any other means."
